# mcs scheduled reconcile (safe tier) - example crontab entry.
#
# The safe tier is additive only: it backfills frontmatter, rebuilds the index,
# and (when implemented) queues proposals to log.md. It NEVER edits prose.
#
# Copy the line below into your crontab (`crontab -e`), adjusting VAULT and the
# path to the mcs binary. This example runs every day at 07:00.
#
#   0 7 * * *  cd /path/to/your-vault && /usr/local/bin/mcs reconcile . >> .mcs/reconcile.log 2>&1
#
# Notes:
# - Use an absolute path to the mcs binary; cron has a minimal PATH.
# - Commit the result on a branch if you want the diff reviewable before it lands
#   on main; the safe tier is designed to produce a clean, additive-only diff.
# - For launchd on macOS, wrap the same command in a LaunchAgent plist with
#   StartCalendarInterval instead of cron.
